case 1: the record only, before the exchange
not exchanged

case 2: after the first move
exchanged

case 3: after the second move
exchanged

case 4: after the third move
exchanged

case 5: a leftover temporary record and a leftover probe file
not exchanged

case 6: the record only, and a metadata file that changed after it
not exchanged

case 7: the temporary file, and a metadata file with neither of the recorded contents
CORRUPTED_DATA
.a.sql.exchange
the temporary file is left

case 8: an exchange between two databases, the database with the copy of the record attached first
exchanged

case 9: a stale copy of a record, whose primary a newer exchange overwrote
a and c exchanged
b unchanged

